+# code-review — cycle 0
+MINOR | e2e/step-definitions/oauth/portal-rename-device.steps.ts:392 | When FOREIGN_USER has no `users` row, the "another user's device" half of scenario 3 is silently dropped (annotation only) and only the unknown-id case runs; coverage depends on leftover state | Make it deterministic: insert the foreign `users` row in the fixture (or sign the foreign user in once) and fail instead of degrading
+INFO | server/lib/nebu/oauth/account.ex:807 | Deviation accepted: a POST to /account/devices/rename without a session answers 302 via start_login (ATDD test pins 302), while every other account POST answers 303 /account. No auth bypass (no write, binding cookie per state, per-source cap on login requests), but it is an inconsistency with the "a POST cannot be replayed through the IdP" rule | Optionally record the reason in the story Decisions
+INFO | server/lib/nebu/oauth/account.ex:965 | Deviation accepted: stale / freshness_unavailable / device_name_invalid redirect (303) to the rename page with the notice; the AC asks for 303 + notice + "Confirm it is you" link and "the form shown again", which the rename page delivers (tests assert notice + reauth link on the landed page). A foreign id with a valid format lands on device_not_found via render_rename, no leak | -
+INFO | server/lib/nebu/oauth/account.ex:239 | The reauth link on the rename page returns to the devices list (`reauth_href(@devices_list, nil)`), not to the rename page; the user must click Rename again after re-authenticating (return_target only knows the five actions) | Follow-up: allow a rename return target
+INFO | server/lib/nebu/oauth/account.ex:950 | Logger.info logs user_id and device_id only, never the name; same pattern as the device sign-out / consent withdraw lines. No name in any log path (DeviceKeyStore.rename_device and AccountManagement do not log) | -
+INFO | server/lib/nebu/oauth/account.ex:921 | Check order matches delete_device: session -> CSRF + BrowserPost (checked_post) -> auth_time nil -> fresh? -> valid_device_id? -> write; user id only from session; FormPost free_text limited to ["device_name"] on the rename path | -
+INFO | server/lib/nebu/matrix/account_management.ex:160 | ADR-018/020 OK: OAuth calls the new facade Nebu.Matrix.account_rename_device/3; SQL stays in the Matrix domain; the write reuses DeviceKeyStore.rename_device/3 (user-scoped UPDATE + stamp_if_keyed!, covered by the keyed-device oracle test) | -
+INFO | server/lib/nebu/oauth/account_templates/rename.html.eex:13 | `maxlength="64"` counts UTF-16 units, the server limit is 64 code points: names with astral characters (emoji) are capped at fewer typed characters in the browser than the server allows; harmless | -
+INFO | server/lib/nebu/oauth/device_name.ex:91 | Deferred MINOR of story 01 (plan/3): confirmed out of the rename path; rename uses only DeviceName.typed/1 | -
+INFO | e2e/step-definitions/oauth/portal-rename-device.steps.ts:147 | gate-y skip (no auth_time from a real IdP) with annotation + evidence log: accepted epic pattern | -
+INFO | server/test/nebu/oauth/portal_rename_device_test.exs:1 | The AC rule "new name appears in the Allow page's 'replaces your session NAME' line" has no direct test; it reads the same devices.display_name column | Optional: one assertion on the Allow page
